«
@@ Cycling — give a value with an uncertainty its next form, keeping
@@ its unit: a…b → c±d → c±p% → c±σd → a…b.
@@ The first three forms state the same bounds: these steps are
@@ equivalences. The two steps to and from c±σd keep the same digits
@@ but change their meaning, a bound becoming a standard deviation or
@@ the reverse: they correct a value typed in the wrong form, and their
@@ result is tagged "non-equivalent". To turn a bound into a standard
@@ deviation by a law, use Bound→σ instead.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @ A value tagged by an earlier press loses its tag
  If Dup TypeName "tag" == Then DeleteTag End
  → cyx
  «
    @ The value without its unit, and the unit as 1_unit (or 1)
    1 cyx
    If cyx TypeName "unit" == Then Drop Drop 1 cyx →Unit cyx UVal End
    → cyu cyv
    «
      cyv TypeName
      → cyt
      «
        Case
          cyt "range" == cyt "drange" == Or Then
            cyv Cycle 0
          End
          cyt "prange" == Then
            cyv Explode → cyc cyp « cyc cyc Abs cyp * 100 / →σRange » 1
          End
          cyt "uncertain" == Then
            cyv Explode → cyc cyd « cyc cyd - cyc cyd + →Range » 1
          End
          "Cycling: expects a…b, a±b, a±p% or a±σb" DoError
        End
        → cyn
        «
          If cyu TypeName "unit" == Then cyu * End
          If cyn Then "non-equivalent" →Tag End
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
